From 44df1120093471db9c6e81a42e8240824b655bc3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: juanan <juanan@test.com>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 12:21:20 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 02/10] T1: add criteria weighting
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

- Weight from 1 to 10 per criterion, stored through the criterion_weight
  persistent (business rules in local\weights). Criteria without a stored
  weight weigh 1, so existing rubrics need no migration.
- Weights are only saved when submitted: disabling the feature keeps them.
- Changing a weight in a rubric already used for grading requires regrade.
- Editor: weight selector and live percentage (AMD weights_editor, the
  upstream YUI editor is untouched). Graders see "Weight x · y %",
  students do not see weights.
- Fix upstream: update_definition() and edit.php read $data->rubric
  instead of $data->rubricranges, so instances were never marked for
  regrade.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
